-- Phase 6 platform additions (plan 18.2), generated by drizzle-kit:
--
-- * task_files_kind_ck gains `home_seed` (P1: home/memories/MEMORY.md and
--   USER.md, copied into the trial home before launch) and `expected_home`
--   (P2: the memory files a correct agent leaves, overlaid on the seeds for a
--   home check's self-check; never copied into a trial). TASK_FILE_KINDS order.
-- * artifacts gains `root` (P2): `workspace`, or `home`, of which only
--   memories/ is collected (artifacts_home_path_ck). Its default labels every
--   existing row a workspace file, which it is. The unique index becomes
--   (attempt_id, root, path), so memories/MEMORY.md may exist in both roots.
--   artifacts_origin_ck gains `home_seed_unchanged` and `home_seed_modified`,
--   and artifacts_origin_root_ck keeps them to the home and the fixture and
--   document origins to the workspace (`agent` belongs to either).
-- * configuration_versions gains `skill_loading` (P5): `preload` (-s per
--   skill, what every version so far ran) or `on_demand` (no -s, the skills
--   toolset added), which needs at least one skill (the 400 of
--   ConfigurationInputSchema, kept here too).
--
-- ADD COLUMN with a constant default rewrites no row and fires no row
-- trigger, so the 0001 guards are not involved: artifacts stay immutable and
-- frozen configuration versions unchanged, each reading `preload` and
-- `workspace`. A CHECK change fires no trigger either, and every existing
-- row satisfies the new CHECKs (Postgres validates them as they are added).
--
-- The config hash of an existing version stays valid: skill loading enters
-- the hash payload only when it is `on_demand` (configurations/settings.ts,
-- HASH_FORMAT unchanged), so a `preload` version hashes exactly as before and
-- estimates from past attempts still match it.
--
-- Nothing else needs DDL: the launch record's home seed inputs, skill
-- loading and background review intervals, the self-check's `home` mode and
-- expected home files, the new load issue codes and file_check's `root`
-- param all live in jsonb columns without a CHECK.

